WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.680
gods don't always come from greatness

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.200
they aren't always born as gods

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:34.200
some gods arrived from far away and no
one sees their ascension coming

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:55.620
Some Gods earn their godhood even when no one else believes
they can

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:02.550
Adam Armada Lindgren was born on March 28 1993 and Gothenburg Sweden
Armada was born into a large family the

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:07.680
fifth of ten siblings and it was through
them that he discovered smash his older

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:13.320
brother Alexander any Olas Lindgren took
him to a local tournament in 2004 which

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:17.340
kicked off his love of competitive super
smash bros melee originally I started

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.580
playing smash 64
it was my older brother and Aeolus olds

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:26.130
my former teammate he borrowed smash64 from a friend of his and we liked

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:31.350
the game so when Melee came out it was very natural for us to buy that game and we

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:35.670
play it in a casual way for a few years
and then an Eolas heard about an

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:39.959
upcoming tournament very close to
where we live so he asked me if I want

00:01:39.959 --> 00:01:43.289
to tag along and I've always loved
competing and I will always love melee

00:01:43.289 --> 00:01:48.240
so that's pretty much how it all started
but while Armada did not succeed at

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:53.610
first he kept pushing two years later he
switched mains from Mars to peach and

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:57.899
started beating his local rivals I feel
like it started off pretty slowly at

00:01:57.899 --> 00:02:01.890
first we were not that many players in
Sweden like tournaments it happened

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:06.869
roughly had like 30 people maybe
eventually a year one and a half year

00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:10.649
and I climbed up to top ten but I said
it was not that many players to begin

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:14.780
with but then it went to a tournament in
early 2007 which was roughly two years

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:19.140
after my first tournament and going into
the tournament that was a marth mained I

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.260
mained marth for roughly one and a half
years

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:26.700
and I walked away from that tournament
as a peach main because that tournament I

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:30.870
did end up having a few matches in a row
where it made more sense for me to play

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:35.610
peach I remember playing as IBP in
losers at some point and an Eolas

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:39.390
already played against him in pools and
beat him with his peach it was like yeah

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.970
Adam I think you should play your peach
instead your marth I think that's

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:46.319
gonna be the right call but being a
local legend was not enough he wanted

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:50.430
more Armada attended Renaissance of
smash four the European national

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:54.690
tournament he knew he wasn't strong
enough to win but he learned something

00:02:54.690 --> 00:03:00.000
important there we always had like once
a year renaissance of smash and it was like

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.290
basically like the European Championship
and that was coming up in July that year

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:08.310
so I had a few more months to practice
and I start to feel very confident I

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:11.970
kind of look at it like you know when
you have a puzzle and you've been

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:15.569
putting enough pieces together and it
all makes sense you know where to put

00:03:15.569 --> 00:03:19.109
the next pieces that kind of what it
felt like for me and Melee it was like

00:03:19.109 --> 00:03:24.329
I had enough of an understanding of the
game where each next step felt very like

00:03:24.329 --> 00:03:27.780
much easier than before he took the
lessons he learned from Renaissance of

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:33.120
smash to heart he kept working never
giving up Armada placed third at the epita

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:38.489
smash arena 2 Europe's biggest melee
tournament then he placed first at smash

00:03:38.489 --> 00:03:41.370
attack which Armada won from the losers
bracket

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:46.139
Armada returned to France for epita
smash arena 3 placing first again

00:03:46.139 --> 00:03:51.389
beating AMSA once more while cementing
his place as Europe's best Smasher but

00:03:51.389 --> 00:03:55.379
it was not enough Europe scene was
smaller than North America's and players

00:03:55.379 --> 00:03:59.010
rarely traveled between regions to
compete in smash tournament's prize

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:04.019
pools were low especially in Europe and
few smash players could rely on melee as

00:04:04.019 --> 00:04:08.400
a full-time job but North America was
where the best players were and Armada

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.359
wanted to prove that he was among the
game's elite going to the US was very

00:04:12.359 --> 00:04:16.169
expensive and I actually ended up
borrowing like $1,000 from my

00:04:16.169 --> 00:04:19.370
grandparents because I was like I want
to go to the US at least once because

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:24.180
melee was not in the strongest state
especially not in 2008 it had a very

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:27.599
rough period of time I was like you
never know how long the game is gonna be

00:04:27.599 --> 00:04:30.370
around I want to be able to go at least
once

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:35.560
and before Genesis the best player in
Europe had never competed with the best

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:39.699
Americans so a lot of to US players
they're like oh no Armada he's not good

00:04:39.699 --> 00:04:44.380
he's not gonna make top 32, some people
thought I was gonna struggle in pools

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:49.120
but for me I was using all of these
words as motivation I was like

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:54.580
alright now I'm gonna practice harder
and then when I perform well I can

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:58.900
literally say that you you and you
you're wrong at the time Genesis was the

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:03.940
largest melee tournament ever held and
the competition was fierce the era we

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:08.530
now know as the era of the five gods was
just beginning and almost every top

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:12.610
player was in attendance on his way to
the grand finals Armada brought down

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:17.919
lucky dishes Wiz mew2king and even
defeated mango America's best player in

00:05:17.919 --> 00:05:21.699
the winners finals but mango was not
going down without a fight

00:05:21.699 --> 00:05:26.979
he beat hungrybox in the losers finals
for another shot at Armada and he made

00:05:26.979 --> 00:05:29.280
it count

00:05:36.259 --> 00:05:40.740
playing that match I was like you know
pretty much singing along this song I

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:44.129
was like so relaxed I was like
regardless of what happens at this point

00:05:44.129 --> 00:05:48.870
I know that I performed well Europe will
be proud I still obviously tried to win

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:54.809
but it was kind of a relief that now
I've proved myself enough so now I

00:05:54.809 --> 00:05:59.099
should not feel as much pressure Armada
made Europe proud and remained

00:05:59.099 --> 00:06:03.029
undefeated when he returned home but
every time he crossed the pond he

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:05.249
couldn't put together a first-place
finish

00:06:05.249 --> 00:06:11.610
he placed 4th at pound 4 2nd at Apex
2010 and second at pound 5 he was

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:15.419
winning everything in Europe but it was
not enough he was beating almost

00:06:15.419 --> 00:06:18.689
everyone in North America but it was not
enough

00:06:18.689 --> 00:06:25.680
he was second and it was still not
enough Armada returned to America for

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:33.449
Genesis 2 in July 2011 and beat bizarro
flame then s2 j and then ppmd hungrybox

00:06:33.449 --> 00:06:38.430
and taj on his way to a faded Grand
Finals rematch with America's best

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:43.169
there's a really good storyline Genesis
2 mango is kind of coming back to melee

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:47.009
again he had a period of time when he
played Mario Captain Falcon was not

00:06:47.009 --> 00:06:50.249
really taking the game too seriously
more going to events to hang out with

00:06:50.249 --> 00:06:55.020
people so it was a good storyline there
as well because I still hadn't managed

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:59.939
to win a super major in the US I got 2nd
multiple times and now mango is back as

00:06:59.939 --> 00:07:03.990
well and then when dropping Grand Finals
again so I think a lot of people were

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:07.319
very happy about the rematch because we
hadn't played a single tournament match

00:07:07.319 --> 00:07:11.999
against each other in those two years in
singles for the first time ever a

00:07:11.999 --> 00:07:16.439
European Smasher took first place on
American soil for the first time ever

00:07:16.439 --> 00:07:21.209
Armada defeated mango in the grand
finals for the first time in the US

00:07:21.209 --> 00:07:30.540
Armada was not second

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:36.090
but still it was not enough armada
kept winning and did not drop a single

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:42.690
tournament from Genesis in July 2011 to
Apex 2013 in January of 2013 Armada

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:47.660
became a god of melee but it gets lonely
on Mount Olympus

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:56.010
even though Armada kept winning even
though he was all but unstoppable melee

00:07:56.010 --> 00:08:00.120
was stagnating back home armada was
on his own and he was getting frustrated

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:05.630
just one week after winning apax he
announced his retirement

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:10.770
it felt pointless after a while I was
like I had proven myself for a long

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:14.730
period of time like I think I was
number one for like one and a half year

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:18.840
or something and I won three super
majors back-to-back so it's basically

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:25.800
like I need to do this for six months to
get like two days of like enjoyment and

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:30.810
after a while I just didn't feel worth
it so I didn't stop playing melee for

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:35.460
that year because I didn't like the game
it was just like I felt like it's not

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:39.450
worth it when I have no one to play
against while Armada was retired in Europe

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:44.760
smash was exploding in the u.s. in
February smashers won a charity donation

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:50.580
drive that got melee back into evo for
the first time since 2007 in October

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:55.650
Travis samox Beauchamp released the
smash brothers a documentary detailing

00:08:55.650 --> 00:09:00.480
the history of melee up to that point
but Armada wasn't competing in European

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.740
tournaments he wasn't seriously testing
his mettle against America's finest

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:09.690
instead he was spending his time working
as a substitute teacher in Sweden

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:15.390
If a teacher was sick they called me in and I was taking over his or her classes for the day

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:19.020
it was never anything I was planning to

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:22.590
do long term it was more like a
part-time job while I was trying to

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:25.939
figure out what I wanted to do with life
but then

00:09:25.939 --> 00:09:31.939
no one quits melee entirely like no one
does so eventually I got you know

00:09:31.939 --> 00:09:37.129
motivated to come back interest in melee
was at an all-time high and armada

00:09:37.129 --> 00:09:41.539
realized that it was finally time to
take the game seriously again armada

00:09:41.539 --> 00:09:46.939
still flew out to Evo and apex 2013 that
year he only played doubles at Apex 2013

00:09:46.939 --> 00:09:51.409
but he placed fourth at Evo he was
floored by the outpouring of passion

00:09:51.409 --> 00:09:55.669
from the community like when I stopped
playing melee I was number one in the

00:09:55.669 --> 00:09:59.959
world for quite a while but when I came
back I kind of struggled for a while

00:09:59.959 --> 00:10:04.549
partly like I barely played for a year
and everyone else got so much better I

00:10:04.549 --> 00:10:08.989
had a lot of catching up to do for sure
and I was also going through depression

00:10:08.989 --> 00:10:14.449
myself at the time so that combined with
all the pressure and expectations like I

00:10:14.449 --> 00:10:17.539
feel like went a lot of other players
have been coming back from a longer

00:10:17.539 --> 00:10:22.879
break it's always been more of like
explanations for why but I feel like for

00:10:22.879 --> 00:10:25.819
me for some reason it was never these
kind of things it was like the first

00:10:25.819 --> 00:10:30.919
tournament I entered it was like a lot
of people expected me to like be back

00:10:30.919 --> 00:10:34.849
as number one immediately Armada
seriously returned to competitive melee

00:10:34.849 --> 00:10:40.009
in time for beast 4 where he placed
second he traveled around Europe winning

00:10:40.009 --> 00:10:43.759
tournament after tournament on his way
back to reclaim his throne but things

00:10:43.759 --> 00:10:48.709
were more difficult than they seemed
2014 was a very bad year for me overall

00:10:48.709 --> 00:10:56.259
to be honest your Avalon 3 singles melee
champion is none other

00:10:56.259 --> 00:11:02.720
Ct EMP armadas returned to the US was
bumpy at first with a fourth place

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:08.839
finish at Skate r3 they saw him lose to
PPMD and mew2king but Armada righted the

00:11:08.839 --> 00:11:16.429
course he beat m2k for first at
super-sweet then defeated him again at

00:11:16.429 --> 00:11:20.019
super smash Sunday's lock-in

00:11:24.019 --> 00:11:30.720
at MLG Anaheim Armada faced off against
mango once again losing three to two in

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:35.670
the winners finals he made it back to
the grand finals but once again mango brought him down

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:55.410
at CEO 2014 mango and
Armada faced off in the grand finals

00:11:55.410 --> 00:12:04.170
again but our mana came out on top
our bata is the champion of CEO 2014

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:08.880
only to fall to mango at King's of Cali
4 a week later the next week

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:13.410
at Evo 2014 armada didn't even get a
chance to play mango as he fell to

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:18.300
hungrybox in both the winter semi finals
and losers finals perhaps it was an omen

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:23.040
of things to come for the two but armadas
main rival was still mango armada

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:27.420
return to Europe defeated but he was
once again unstoppable on his home turf

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:31.709
his career had come full circle he was
the best in Europe but couldn't quite

00:12:31.709 --> 00:12:36.269
make it past the last hoop stateside in
November 2014 Armada signed with

00:12:36.269 --> 00:12:40.980
Alliance following a lower than usual
fourth place finish at big house four

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:46.050
I feel bad about that performance I am a
very very competitive person yes if I do

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:49.620
not place first that's not enough for me
yeah which second place is no good

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:52.350
that's no good which means fourth place
is horrible

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:57.180
then Armada fell to fifth at Paragon
Orlando his lowest placement since the

00:12:57.180 --> 00:13:05.760
early days of his career Armada

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:09.000
from that point forward something changed in Armada
whatever last piece of the puzzle was

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:13.860
missing he found it whatever training
needed doing he did it whatever he did

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:17.029
it was enough

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:37.029
Armada took second at Apex 2015 first at
MVG sandstorm second at CEO 2015 first

00:13:37.029 --> 00:13:43.689
at Evo 2015 first at the big house five
first at Smash summit first at Genesis 3

00:13:43.689 --> 00:13:49.269
and first at Smash summit 2 Armada
was without question the best melee

00:13:49.269 --> 00:13:56.139
player in the world yet again when I won
evo 2015 my life overall was so much

00:13:56.139 --> 00:14:02.110
better I was in a much better place I've
been dating my girlfriend for five

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:07.240
months at the time as well and when I
start to feel better as a human being I

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:11.379
could see that in melee as well I
started to perform much better and once

00:14:11.379 --> 00:14:16.480
i won EVO it was also like a big
relief it was like I still can win super

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:22.480
majors and once I did that it was just
so much easier to like keep performing

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:28.720
well then came Evo 2016 Armada was
looking strong but hungrybox always a

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:33.220
step behind him shocked the world with a
grand finals reset and took an upset

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:37.170
victory on melees biggest stage

00:14:56.119 --> 00:15:02.009
yeah it was one of my absolute toughest
losses it's probably my second toughest

00:15:02.009 --> 00:15:06.419
loss of all time next to pound five
actually but yeah it was very rough like

00:15:06.419 --> 00:15:10.499
I wanted to also tie up the two Evo's
say I wanted to win that second Evo

00:15:10.499 --> 00:15:14.309
title and also felt like I had it in the
bag which also makes it way harder to

00:15:14.309 --> 00:15:19.410
lose if you lose a set very convincingly
 you might be disappointed that you

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:23.329
didn't play good enough and stuff but if
you lose 3-2 especially when you're up

00:15:23.329 --> 00:15:30.359
in the final game it's it's much tougher
to accept that so yeah it was a very

00:15:30.359 --> 00:15:34.589
emotional loss for me but hbox play
fantastic that day and he deserved it

00:15:34.589 --> 00:15:39.179
and he probably wanted it even more than
I wanted especially since he got 2nd

00:15:39.179 --> 00:15:42.720
twice in a row so yeah he earned that
one

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:48.449
but Armada bounced back first at
Canada Cup 2016 first at smash summit 3

00:15:48.449 --> 00:15:55.079
first at Dreamhack winter 2016 first at
the UGC smash open first at Genesis 4

00:15:55.079 --> 00:16:02.249
first at Beast 7 first at smash summit
again first at evil 2017 with plenty of

00:16:02.249 --> 00:16:07.069
tournaments in between even make it back

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:14.439
oh my god the repeat of world war, 3-1
armada

00:16:14.439 --> 00:16:21.040
winning evo 2017 from winners armadas
back half of 2017 has been difficult

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:25.300
hungrybox has caught up to the swedish
sniper and other top players started

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:28.160
figuring things out but armada will
bounce back

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:32.920
he always has and he always will and
when he does someone will have to get

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:40.760
even better to beat him because for
armada, second is never enough

